# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This git repository is rooted at your HOME directory (C:\Users\Hp).
# That is unusual and dangerous: a plain `git add .` here would try to stage your
# ENTIRE home folder — including secrets such as .git-credentials, .aws/ tokens,
# and .claude.json — into a repo that pushes to a public GitHub remote.
#
# To prevent that, we ignore EVERYTHING by default and then explicitly re-include
# only the project this repo is meant to track (Desktop/hackathon-5).
#
# To start tracking something new, add a `!/path` exception — remembering to
# un-ignore each parent directory, exactly as done for Desktop/hackathon-5 below.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1) Ignore every top-level entry in the home directory.
/*

# 2) Keep this .gitignore file and the repo landing README trackable.
!/.gitignore
!/README.md

# 3) Re-include ONLY Desktop/hackathon-5 (the project this repo tracks).
!/Desktop/
/Desktop/*
!/Desktop/hackathon-5/
